description:
## Finding

uuencoding/src/lib.rs uses double-hash headings in doc comments:
  /// ## Errors
  ///
  /// - [UuError::InvalidBeginLine] ...
  ///
  /// ## Partial results
  ///
  /// ...
  ///
  /// ## Examples

yencoding/src/lib.rs uses single-hash headings:
  /// # Errors
  ///
  /// - [YencError::NoHeader] ...
  ///
  /// # Examples

## Impact

In rustdoc HTML output, ## headings render as <h3> (one level below the implicit <h2> of named sections), while # headings render as <h2>. The yencoding docs follow the standard rustdoc convention (single # for Errors, Panics, Examples, Safety is idiomatic and recommended). The uuencoding docs use double ## which renders them at a deeper level than the standard sections, making the docs visually inconsistent between crates when viewed side-by-side in docs.rs.
